From 2e73a605a866e3e10cee2d53d7ce46513ff57e5b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 13:31:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] lifecycle guard: scan uv run, py/pypy and programs
 fed on stdin

`python3 f.py` (f.py runs `hermes gateway restart`) was refused, but the same file ran unread
as `uv run f.py`, `uv run python f.py`, `py f.py`, `pypy3 f.py`, `python3 < f.py`,
`cat f.py | python3`, `bash < f.sh` and `cat f.sh | bash`. Found in the exact-head review of
PR #2165 (review 5890466338). The reserved-word half of that finding (`do`/`then`/`!`/`{`)
landed separately in 12cca5b455; this change covers the runners and stdin feeds it does not.

Why: the interpreter scan matched only `python[w][N]` at the executed command, `uv` was not a
wrapper, `_python_script_operand` treated "no operand" as nothing to read, and the shell walk
read a shell's script operand but never the file redirected or piped into its stdin.

Fix (additive; no existing reference is removed):
- `uv [opts] run [opts] <cmd>` peels like a transparent wrapper (`_peel_uv_run`); `uv pip`,
  `uv tool run` and `uvx` do not. A `.py` reached through `uv run` is read by the interpreter
  scan as Python, and skipped by the shell walk (Python sources are never shell-walked, #77131).
- `_PYTHON_RUNNER_RE` adds `py` and `pypy[N]` to the interpreter scan.
- `_split_redirections` strips redirections from the argv tail and returns `<`/`<>` stdin files;
  `_iter_segment_contexts` carries the operands of a `cat` piped into the segment. A Python or a
  shell with no program operand (or `-s`) scans those files as its program.
- `_PIPE_TO_INTERPRETER` also matches a pipe into python/pypy/py/uv, so a data sink feeding one
  is not masked.

Tests: tests/cron/test_lifecycle_guard_interpreter_runners.py, 58 cases (runner spellings,
stdin and pipe feeds, combined with reserved words), plus mention/data guards (`uv pip`,
`uvx`, `python3 clean.py < f.py`, `cat f | grep`, `while read; done < f`) and the #77131
not-shell-walked rule. RED on base e770862093: 38 failed, 20 passed. GREEN: all pass.
